  "worked_solution": "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3x+9y \\\\ 6x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n    Therefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
